  "body": "#2516: in a group of value fields, Enter did not move the focus to the next value field, and Tab seemed not to move it either.\n\n## What I found\n\negui's own Tab moved the focus, but in draw order over each focusable widget. On the operation property panel, Tab from a value field went to:\n\n- a group header (it has no visible focus mark), then\n- a checkbox or a combo, then\n- the action bar: Generate, Clear toolpath, Close and Delete operation.\n\nThus the focus seemed to leave the form. Enter committed the value and dropped the focus (egui's default for a DragValue).\n\n## What changed\n\n- New `crates/ui/src/egui_app/layout/field_ring.rs`: a ring of the value fields of the Properties pane.\n  - The form seam's number helpers in `fields.rs` register each field (`num`, `num_feed`, `num_narrow`, the `num_*_row`/`_named`/`_by` forms, `num_plain`, `int_range_row`, `num_unit`).\n  - `group_open` (`layout/form.rs`) marks the group of the fields in its body.\n  - `pages::properties` opens the ring before the pane and closes it after.\n- From a registered field:\n  - Tab moves to the next field, and Shift+Tab to the previous one. The ring wraps at the two ends.\n  - Enter commits the value to the draft (as before) and moves to the next field of the same group. After the group's last field, the focus drops (as before).\n  - From a combo, a checkbox or a button, egui's own order stays.\n- The moved-to field gets the focus when the next frame begins, before any widget draws. Thus egui's DragValue selects its text, and a typed number replaces the old one, as after a click. A repaint is requested for that frame.\n- Focus is ephemeral UI state and queues no command. A value still reaches the document only through Apply (`EditOperationParams`).\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/2516-field-focus.md`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `egui_app::field_focus_tests` (new, on the real operation property panel of a Pocket op):\n  - `tab_and_shift_tab_walk_the_value_fields_and_wrap` (Heights): Tab goes 25 → 12 → 9 → 1 → 25, past the combos and the group headers. Shift+Tab wraps from the first field to the last, then goes back. No command is queued.\n  - `enter_commits_the_value_and_moves_to_the_next_field_of_its_group` (Feeds): a typed 750 lands in the draft, and the focus moves to the plunge feed. A typed 150 there replaces the old value. The document keeps 800 until Apply. Enter in the group's last field drops the focus.\n- `egui_app::layout::field_ring::tests` (3): the pure rule (wrap, Enter within the group only, no move from a widget outside the ring).\n- Mutation check: with the ring's move switched off, both panel tests fail.\n- Changed: the `thread_hand_tests` helpers `edit_number` and `type_dip` click a field only when it is not focused. After Enter, the next field already has the focus with its text selected. A click on a focused field only places the cursor, so the typed text was appended.\n\nGates on 213874858:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 9 steps, 0 failed (`ui lib` and the 7 UI suites of the gate map). The last edit after the gate is a clippy fix (`Option::replace`), with the same behaviour. The `field_` and `thread_hand` tests (18) are green after it.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- No snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No hand test in the real window. The tests drive the real `pages::properties` code through the harness.\n- Fields drawn with a raw `DragValue` outside the form seam helpers are not in the ring. egui's own Tab order stays for them (#1122 moves the pages to the seam).\n- Dialogs outside the Properties pane (for example the tool library window) are not in the ring.\n\nChangelog: In the Properties pane, Tab and Shift+Tab move between the value fields, and Enter commits a value and moves to the next field of its group (#2516)\n\nEffort: medium (the label of the issue). Not escalated.\n\nFixes #2516\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
